## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical data structure design for a common gaming feature, balancing efficient updates with query performance.

## Key Concepts
- Hash maps provide O(1) player score lookups
- Ordered maps enable range and top-k access
- Ordered sets handle duplicate scores within groups
- Rank computation accounts for tied scores

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode illustrating approach
class Leaderboard {
  constructor(){
    this.playerToScore = new Map();
    this.scoreToPlayers = new Map(); // descending keys; each maps to a Set of players
  }
  addOrUpdate(playerId, score) {
    // Remove from old score group if exists
    const oldScore = this.playerToScore.get(playerId);
    if (oldScore !== undefined) {
      const oldSet = this.scoreToPlayers.get(oldScore);
      oldSet.delete(playerId);
      if (oldSet.size === 0) this.scoreToPlayers.delete(oldScore);
    }
    // Update maps and add to new score group
    this.playerToScore.set(playerId, score);
    if (!this.scoreToPlayers.has(score)) {
      this.scoreToPlayers.set(score, new Set());
    }
    this.scoreToPlayers.get(score).add(playerId);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Dynamic connectivity with insertions and deletions is a classic hard problem. This offline approach tests understanding of edge lifetimes and versioning, and how to combine segment trees with DSU rollback for log-scale updates.

## Key Concepts
- DSU with rollback (no path compression) to enable undo.
- Segment tree over time to map edge active intervals to time ranges.
- Offline processing: traverse tree, apply unions, answer leaf queries, then rollback.

## Code Example
```javascript
class RollbackDSU {
  constructor(n){
    this.parent = Array.from({length:n}, (_,i)=>i);
    this.sz = Array(n).fill(1);
    this.ch = [];
  }
  find(x){ while (this.parent[x]!==x) x = this.parent[x]; return x; }
  union(a,b){
    a = this.find(a); b = this.find(b);
    if (a===b){ this.ch.push(null); return; }
    if (this.sz[a] < this.sz[b]) [a,b] = [b,a];
    this.ch.push([b, this.parent[b], a, this.sz[a]]);
    this.parent[b] = a; this.sz[a] += this.sz[b];
  }
  snapshot(){ return this.ch.length; }
  rollback(snap){
    while (this.ch.length > snap){
      const ch = this.ch.pop();
      if (!ch) continue;
      const [b, oldP, a, oldS] = ch;
      this.parent[b] = oldP; this.sz[a] = oldS;
    }
  }
}
```

